{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ember-hotkeys"},{"type":"text","value":" with the "},{"type":"link","href":"../../installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"installation instructions"}]},{"type":"text","value":". This guide builds a save shortcut and shows the component lifecycle used by the other APIs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"your-first-hotkey","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your first hotkey"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a strict-mode "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".gts"},{"type":"text","value":" component. Import the template helper into that file."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { tracked } from '@glimmer/tracking'\nimport { on } from '@ember/modifier'\nimport { useHotkey, formatForDisplay } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class Editor extends Component {\n\t@tracked count = 0\n\t@tracked enabled = true\n\tsave = () => this.count++\n\ttoggle = () => { this.enabled = !this.enabled }\n\tlabel = formatForDisplay('Mod+S')\n\n\t<template>\n\t\t{{useHotkey 'Mod+S' this.save enabled=this.enabled}}\n\t\t<button type=\"button\" {{on 'click' this.toggle}}>Toggle shortcut</button>\n\t\t<p>Press <kbd>{{this.label}}</kbd>. Saved {{this.count}} times.</p>\n\t</template>\n}","lang":"gts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Press Command+S on macOS or Control+S on Windows and Linux. The count increases and the browser save dialog is prevented. The toggle disables execution while preserving the registration."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves to the primary platform modifier. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Mod+[KeyS]"},{"type":"text","value":" instead when the shortcut must follow the physical S position."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"registration-and-cleanup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Registration and cleanup"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkey"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeys"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeySequence"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeySequences"},{"type":"text","value":" are template helpers. Invoke them with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{{...}}"},{"type":"text","value":", not as JavaScript hooks. Tracked arguments update registrations after rendering. Removing a helper from the template unregisters its bindings."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State readers and recorders are JavaScript functions. Pass the containing component as their first argument, usually "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this"},{"type":"text","value":". The adapter releases subscriptions and recorders when that owner is destroyed. State readers expose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".value"},{"type":"text","value":"; recorder fields and registration arrays are reactive getters. Read those properties in templates or getters instead of destructuring an initial snapshot."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"common-patterns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Common patterns"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"multiple-hotkeys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multiple hotkeys"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{{useHotkey 'Mod+S' this.save}}\n{{useHotkey 'Mod+Z' this.undo}}\n{{useHotkey 'Mod+Shift+Z' this.redo}}","lang":"hbs"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each registration is independent. For a dynamic list, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeys"},{"type":"text","value":" as shown in the "},{"type":"link","href":"./guides/hotkeys.md#registering-multiple-hotkeys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hotkeys guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"scoped-hotkeys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scoped hotkeys"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onHotkey"},{"type":"text","value":" and attach it to the element. It handles registration, reactive options, and cleanup with the element's lifecycle."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<div tabindex=\"0\" {{onHotkey 'Escape' this.close enabled=this.enabled}}>\n\tFocus here and press Escape.\n</div>","lang":"hbs"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onHotkeys"},{"type":"text","value":" for an array of definitions. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./guides/hotkeys.md#target","children":[{"type":"text","value":"complete scoped example"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"conditional-hotkeys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Conditional hotkeys"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{{useHotkey 'Mod+S' this.save enabled=this.enabled}}","lang":"hbs"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use Ember tracked state for the enabled flag."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"multi-key-sequences","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Multi-key sequences"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{{useHotkeySequence (array 'G' 'G') this.goToTop}}","lang":"hbs"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"array"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@ember/helper"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useHotkeySequence"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ember-hotkeys"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Release G between presses. Automatic key repeats do not advance sequences."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tracking-held-keys-and-displaying-hints","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tracking held keys and displaying hints"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { useHeldKeys, useHeldKeyCodes, useKeyHold, useHotkeyHint } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class KeyStatus extends Component {\n\theld = useHeldKeys(this)\n\tcodes = useHeldKeyCodes(this)\n\tshift = useKeyHold(this, 'Shift')\n\thint = useHotkeyHint(this, 'Mod+S')\n\n\tget keys() { return this.held.value.join(' + ') || 'No keys held' }\n\tget shiftCode() { return this.codes.value.Shift ?? 'Not held' }\n\n\t<template>\n\t\t<p>{{this.keys}}</p>\n\t\t<p>Shift position: {{this.shiftCode}}</p>\n\t\t{{#if this.shift.value}}<button type=\"button\">Delete permanently</button>{{/if}}\n\t\t{{#if this.hint.value}}<kbd>Save</kbd>{{/if}}\n\t</template>\n}","lang":"gts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"formatForDisplay(binding)"},{"type":"text","value":" for platform-specific labels. Keep the original binding in state; a display label is not a registration string."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"shared-defaults","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared defaults"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createHotkeysScope"},{"type":"text","value":". The scope accepts "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hotkey"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hotkeySequence"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hotkeyRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"hotkeySequenceRecorder"},{"type":"text","value":" options. Use the returned contextual helpers, modifiers, and recorder factories. Pass the scope through component arguments to share it with descendants; helpers and recorders still clean up with their own owners. Pass a getter for tracked defaults. Call-specific options override scope defaults, and per-definition options override common options. Omitted options use the core defaults."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { tracked } from '@glimmer/tracking'\nimport { createHotkeysScope } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class Editor extends Component {\n  @tracked enabled = true\n  hotkeys = createHotkeysScope(() => ({\n    hotkey: { enabled: this.enabled, requireReset: true },\n    hotkeySequence: { timeout: 1500 },\n    hotkeyRecorder: { ignoreInputs: false },\n    hotkeySequenceRecorder: { idleTimeoutMs: 2000 },\n  }))\n  save = () => console.log('Saved')\n  next = () => console.log('Next')\n\n  <template>\n    {{this.hotkeys.useHotkey 'Mod+S' this.save}}\n    {{this.hotkeys.useHotkey 'ArrowRight' this.next requireReset=false}}\n  </template>\n}","lang":"gts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A child can receive this scope as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@hotkeys={{this.hotkeys}}"},{"type":"text","value":" and call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{{@hotkeys.useHotkey ...}}"},{"type":"text","value":". To use recorder defaults, call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this.hotkeys.useHotkeyRecorder(this, options)"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this.hotkeys.useHotkeySequenceRecorder(this, options)"},{"type":"text","value":". The standalone imports use core defaults. The scope itself owns no registrations and needs no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"destroy()"},{"type":"text","value":" call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples-and-next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples and next steps"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./guides/hotkeys","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hotkeys"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./guides/sequences","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sequences"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./guides/hotkey-recording","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hotkey recording"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./guides/sequence-recording","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sequence recording"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./guides/key-state-tracking","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Key state tracking"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./guides/formatting-display","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Formatting and display"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./examples/kitchen-sink","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kitchen sink"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./reference/index","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API reference"}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"your-first-hotkey","text":"Your first hotkey","level":2},{"id":"registration-and-cleanup","text":"Registration and cleanup","level":2},{"id":"common-patterns","text":"Common patterns","level":2},{"id":"multiple-hotkeys","text":"Multiple hotkeys","level":3},{"id":"scoped-hotkeys","text":"Scoped hotkeys","level":3},{"id":"conditional-hotkeys","text":"Conditional hotkeys","level":3},{"id":"multi-key-sequences","text":"Multi-key sequences","level":3},{"id":"tracking-held-keys-and-displaying-hints","text":"Tracking held keys and displaying hints","level":3},{"id":"shared-defaults","text":"Shared defaults","level":2},{"id":"examples-and-next-steps","text":"Examples and next steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nInstall `@tanstack/ember-hotkeys` with the [installation instructions](../../installation). This guide builds a save shortcut and shows the component lifecycle used by the other APIs.\n\n## Your first hotkey\n\nUse a strict-mode `.gts` component. Import the template helper into that file.\n\n```gts\nimport Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { tracked } from '@glimmer/tracking'\nimport { on } from '@ember/modifier'\nimport { useHotkey, formatForDisplay } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class Editor extends Component {\n\t@tracked count = 0\n\t@tracked enabled = true\n\tsave = () => this.count++\n\ttoggle = () => { this.enabled = !this.enabled }\n\tlabel = formatForDisplay('Mod+S')\n\n\t<template>\n\t\t{{useHotkey 'Mod+S' this.save enabled=this.enabled}}\n\t\t<button type=\"button\" {{on 'click' this.toggle}}>Toggle shortcut</button>\n\t\t<p>Press <kbd>{{this.label}}</kbd>. Saved {{this.count}} times.</p>\n\t</template>\n}\n```\n\nPress Command+S on macOS or Control+S on Windows and Linux. The count increases and the browser save dialog is prevented. The toggle disables execution while preserving the registration.\n\n`Mod` resolves to the primary platform modifier. Use `Mod+[KeyS]` instead when the shortcut must follow the physical S position.\n\n## Registration and cleanup\n\n`useHotkey`, `useHotkeys`, `useHotkeySequence`, and `useHotkeySequences` are template helpers. Invoke them with `{{...}}`, not as JavaScript hooks. Tracked arguments update registrations after rendering. Removing a helper from the template unregisters its bindings.\n\nState readers and recorders are JavaScript functions. Pass the containing component as their first argument, usually `this`. The adapter releases subscriptions and recorders when that owner is destroyed. State readers expose `.value`; recorder fields and registration arrays are reactive getters. Read those properties in templates or getters instead of destructuring an initial snapshot.\n\n## Common patterns\n\n### Multiple hotkeys\n\n\n```hbs\n{{useHotkey 'Mod+S' this.save}}\n{{useHotkey 'Mod+Z' this.undo}}\n{{useHotkey 'Mod+Shift+Z' this.redo}}\n```\n\nEach registration is independent. For a dynamic list, use `useHotkeys` as shown in the [hotkeys guide](./guides/hotkeys.md#registering-multiple-hotkeys).\n\n### Scoped hotkeys\n\nImport `onHotkey` and attach it to the element. It handles registration, reactive options, and cleanup with the element's lifecycle.\n\n```hbs\n<div tabindex=\"0\" {{onHotkey 'Escape' this.close enabled=this.enabled}}>\n\tFocus here and press Escape.\n</div>\n```\n\nUse `onHotkeys` for an array of definitions. See the [complete scoped example](./guides/hotkeys.md#target).\n\n### Conditional hotkeys\n\n\n```hbs\n{{useHotkey 'Mod+S' this.save enabled=this.enabled}}\n```\n\nUse Ember tracked state for the enabled flag.\n\n### Multi-key sequences\n\n\n```hbs\n{{useHotkeySequence (array 'G' 'G') this.goToTop}}\n```\n\nImport `array` from `@ember/helper` and `useHotkeySequence` from `@tanstack/ember-hotkeys`.\n\nRelease G between presses. Automatic key repeats do not advance sequences.\n\n### Tracking held keys and displaying hints\n\n\n```gts\nimport Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { useHeldKeys, useHeldKeyCodes, useKeyHold, useHotkeyHint } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class KeyStatus extends Component {\n\theld = useHeldKeys(this)\n\tcodes = useHeldKeyCodes(this)\n\tshift = useKeyHold(this, 'Shift')\n\thint = useHotkeyHint(this, 'Mod+S')\n\n\tget keys() { return this.held.value.join(' + ') || 'No keys held' }\n\tget shiftCode() { return this.codes.value.Shift ?? 'Not held' }\n\n\t<template>\n\t\t<p>{{this.keys}}</p>\n\t\t<p>Shift position: {{this.shiftCode}}</p>\n\t\t{{#if this.shift.value}}<button type=\"button\">Delete permanently</button>{{/if}}\n\t\t{{#if this.hint.value}}<kbd>Save</kbd>{{/if}}\n\t</template>\n}\n```\n\nUse `formatForDisplay(binding)` for platform-specific labels. Keep the original binding in state; a display label is not a registration string.\n\n## Shared defaults\n\nPass defaults to `createHotkeysScope`. The scope accepts `hotkey`, `hotkeySequence`, `hotkeyRecorder`, and `hotkeySequenceRecorder` options. Use the returned contextual helpers, modifiers, and recorder factories. Pass the scope through component arguments to share it with descendants; helpers and recorders still clean up with their own owners. Pass a getter for tracked defaults. Call-specific options override scope defaults, and per-definition options override common options. Omitted options use the core defaults.\n\n```gts\nimport Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { tracked } from '@glimmer/tracking'\nimport { createHotkeysScope } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class Editor extends Component {\n  @tracked enabled = true\n  hotkeys = createHotkeysScope(() => ({\n    hotkey: { enabled: this.enabled, requireReset: true },\n    hotkeySequence: { timeout: 1500 },\n    hotkeyRecorder: { ignoreInputs: false },\n    hotkeySequenceRecorder: { idleTimeoutMs: 2000 },\n  }))\n  save = () => console.log('Saved')\n  next = () => console.log('Next')\n\n  <template>\n    {{this.hotkeys.useHotkey 'Mod+S' this.save}}\n    {{this.hotkeys.useHotkey 'ArrowRight' this.next requireReset=false}}\n  </template>\n}\n```\n\nA child can receive this scope as `@hotkeys={{this.hotkeys}}` and call `{{@hotkeys.useHotkey ...}}`. To use recorder defaults, call `this.hotkeys.useHotkeyRecorder(this, options)` or `this.hotkeys.useHotkeySequenceRecorder(this, options)`. The standalone imports use core defaults. The scope itself owns no registrations and needs no `destroy()` call.\n\n## Examples and next steps\n\n- [Hotkeys](./guides/hotkeys)\n- [Sequences](./guides/sequences)\n- [Hotkey recording](./guides/hotkey-recording)\n- [Sequence recording](./guides/sequence-recording)\n- [Key state tracking](./guides/key-state-tracking)\n- [Formatting and display](./guides/formatting-display)\n- [Kitchen sink](./examples/kitchen-sink)\n- [API reference](./reference/index)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Quick Start\nid: quick-start\n---\n\nInstall `@tanstack/ember-hotkeys` with the [installation instructions](../../installation). This guide builds a save shortcut and shows the component lifecycle used by the other APIs.\n\n## Your first hotkey\n\nUse a strict-mode `.gts` component. Import the template helper into that file.\n\n```gts\nimport Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { tracked } from '@glimmer/tracking'\nimport { on } from '@ember/modifier'\nimport { useHotkey, formatForDisplay } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class Editor extends Component {\n\t@tracked count = 0\n\t@tracked enabled = true\n\tsave = () => this.count++\n\ttoggle = () => { this.enabled = !this.enabled }\n\tlabel = formatForDisplay('Mod+S')\n\n\t<template>\n\t\t{{useHotkey 'Mod+S' this.save enabled=this.enabled}}\n\t\t<button type=\"button\" {{on 'click' this.toggle}}>Toggle shortcut</button>\n\t\t<p>Press <kbd>{{this.label}}</kbd>. Saved {{this.count}} times.</p>\n\t</template>\n}\n```\n\nPress Command+S on macOS or Control+S on Windows and Linux. The count increases and the browser save dialog is prevented. The toggle disables execution while preserving the registration.\n\n`Mod` resolves to the primary platform modifier. Use `Mod+[KeyS]` instead when the shortcut must follow the physical S position.\n\n## Registration and cleanup\n\n`useHotkey`, `useHotkeys`, `useHotkeySequence`, and `useHotkeySequences` are template helpers. Invoke them with `{{...}}`, not as JavaScript hooks. Tracked arguments update registrations after rendering. Removing a helper from the template unregisters its bindings.\n\nState readers and recorders are JavaScript functions. Pass the containing component as their first argument, usually `this`. The adapter releases subscriptions and recorders when that owner is destroyed. State readers expose `.value`; recorder fields and registration arrays are reactive getters. Read those properties in templates or getters instead of destructuring an initial snapshot.\n\n## Common patterns\n\n### Multiple hotkeys\n\n\n```hbs\n{{useHotkey 'Mod+S' this.save}}\n{{useHotkey 'Mod+Z' this.undo}}\n{{useHotkey 'Mod+Shift+Z' this.redo}}\n```\n\nEach registration is independent. For a dynamic list, use `useHotkeys` as shown in the [hotkeys guide](./guides/hotkeys.md#registering-multiple-hotkeys).\n\n### Scoped hotkeys\n\nImport `onHotkey` and attach it to the element. It handles registration, reactive options, and cleanup with the element's lifecycle.\n\n```hbs\n<div tabindex=\"0\" {{onHotkey 'Escape' this.close enabled=this.enabled}}>\n\tFocus here and press Escape.\n</div>\n```\n\nUse `onHotkeys` for an array of definitions. See the [complete scoped example](./guides/hotkeys.md#target).\n\n### Conditional hotkeys\n\n\n```hbs\n{{useHotkey 'Mod+S' this.save enabled=this.enabled}}\n```\n\nUse Ember tracked state for the enabled flag.\n\n### Multi-key sequences\n\n\n```hbs\n{{useHotkeySequence (array 'G' 'G') this.goToTop}}\n```\n\nImport `array` from `@ember/helper` and `useHotkeySequence` from `@tanstack/ember-hotkeys`.\n\nRelease G between presses. Automatic key repeats do not advance sequences.\n\n### Tracking held keys and displaying hints\n\n\n```gts\nimport Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { useHeldKeys, useHeldKeyCodes, useKeyHold, useHotkeyHint } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class KeyStatus extends Component {\n\theld = useHeldKeys(this)\n\tcodes = useHeldKeyCodes(this)\n\tshift = useKeyHold(this, 'Shift')\n\thint = useHotkeyHint(this, 'Mod+S')\n\n\tget keys() { return this.held.value.join(' + ') || 'No keys held' }\n\tget shiftCode() { return this.codes.value.Shift ?? 'Not held' }\n\n\t<template>\n\t\t<p>{{this.keys}}</p>\n\t\t<p>Shift position: {{this.shiftCode}}</p>\n\t\t{{#if this.shift.value}}<button type=\"button\">Delete permanently</button>{{/if}}\n\t\t{{#if this.hint.value}}<kbd>Save</kbd>{{/if}}\n\t</template>\n}\n```\n\nUse `formatForDisplay(binding)` for platform-specific labels. Keep the original binding in state; a display label is not a registration string.\n\n## Shared defaults\n\nPass defaults to `createHotkeysScope`. The scope accepts `hotkey`, `hotkeySequence`, `hotkeyRecorder`, and `hotkeySequenceRecorder` options. Use the returned contextual helpers, modifiers, and recorder factories. Pass the scope through component arguments to share it with descendants; helpers and recorders still clean up with their own owners. Pass a getter for tracked defaults. Call-specific options override scope defaults, and per-definition options override common options. Omitted options use the core defaults.\n\n```gts\nimport Component from '@glimmer/component'\nimport { tracked } from '@glimmer/tracking'\nimport { createHotkeysScope } from '@tanstack/ember-hotkeys'\n\nexport default class Editor extends Component {\n  @tracked enabled = true\n  hotkeys = createHotkeysScope(() => ({\n    hotkey: { enabled: this.enabled, requireReset: true },\n    hotkeySequence: { timeout: 1500 },\n    hotkeyRecorder: { ignoreInputs: false },\n    hotkeySequenceRecorder: { idleTimeoutMs: 2000 },\n  }))\n  save = () => console.log('Saved')\n  next = () => console.log('Next')\n\n  <template>\n    {{this.hotkeys.useHotkey 'Mod+S' this.save}}\n    {{this.hotkeys.useHotkey 'ArrowRight' this.next requireReset=false}}\n  </template>\n}\n```\n\nA child can receive this scope as `@hotkeys={{this.hotkeys}}` and call `{{@hotkeys.useHotkey ...}}`. To use recorder defaults, call `this.hotkeys.useHotkeyRecorder(this, options)` or `this.hotkeys.useHotkeySequenceRecorder(this, options)`. The standalone imports use core defaults. The scope itself owns no registrations and needs no `destroy()` call.\n\n## Examples and next steps\n\n- [Hotkeys](./guides/hotkeys)\n- [Sequences](./guides/sequences)\n- [Hotkey recording](./guides/hotkey-recording)\n- [Sequence recording](./guides/sequence-recording)\n- [Key state tracking](./guides/key-state-tracking)\n- [Formatting and display](./guides/formatting-display)\n- [Kitchen sink](./examples/kitchen-sink)\n- [API reference](./reference/index)\n"}
